					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RESIZE\n\nThe Resize node can be used when you need to resize a texture.\nIn this example we've imported an image that is 32x32 pixels.\nWe use the resize node to resize it to 1920x1080.\n\nThe mode parameter decides how the image will be stretched.\nThe sampling parameter determines how the image will look.\nNearest will be pixelated and sharp, Linear will be smooth and sometimes blurry.\n\nAssignment: have a play with the different mode and sampling options.\n\nThe resolution parameter is currently set to 1x.\nThis means that it will scale to 1 times the patch resolution.\nIf you need manual control over the amount of pixels; click on the Resize node, navigate to the node panel and set the Resolution Mode to absolute.\n\nAssignment: Resize the image to 320x320 pixels using absolute mode.\n"
					}
				},
